WHAT IS NOT PROVEN — and must not drift in the submission
  - Power-loss durability. Crash tests kill the process; they say nothing about
    the disk's own write cache.
  - "0 acknowledged records lost" is measured on the 200-cycle kill -9 suite,
    which is M5 and does not exist yet. Current crash coverage is directory
    snapshots taken mid-run: the same on-disk states, NOT the same claim.
  - No throughput number has been measured. None can be from this machine
    (macOS full-drive flush, PRD 11.2). Benchmarks are Linux-only.
  - Tamper-EVIDENT, not tamper-proof: a consistent rewrite of the whole
    directory is only detectable against an externally held chain head.

INVARIANTS (breaking one is a bug, not a refactor)
  1. Raw bytes are never modified.
  2. Nothing goes downstream before the vault reports durable.
  3. Every queue bounded, every wire-read length capped.
  4. A failed fsync is never retried; the vault goes terminal.
  5. A writer refuses damaged storage; a reader must not (vaultctl verify).
  6. Seal order: footer, fsync, ledger, fsync.
  7. "Sealed" is a valid footer on disk and nothing else.
  8. All timestamps go through record.TimeToNanos.
  9. No time.Now(), map order or goroutines in the generator.
 10. Raw payload is never logged or printed unescaped.
 11. Only measured numbers, with hardware and sync mode.

